---
import Layout from '../layouts/Layout.astro';
import ArcadeCard from '../components/ArcadeCard.astro';
import { games, storyPath } from '../data/arcade';
import '../styles/arcade.css';
import { getCollection } from 'astro:content';
const storyLive = (await getCollection('posts')).some(p => p.id === 'i-just-wanted-to-play-games' && !p.data.draft);
---
<Layout title="The arcade · ProbablyFine" description="The DOS and Macintosh games that got me into computers, playable in your browser. Pick a game and stay awhile.">
  <div class="arcade-shell">
    <section class="arcade-hero">
      <p class="arcade-eyebrow">probablyfine / a few old favourites</p>
      <h1>The arcade<span aria-hidden="true">_</span></h1>
      <p class="arcade-intro">I just wanted to play games. For a long time, that was all I wanted a computer for.</p>
      <p class="arcade-intro-secondary">These are some of the games I remember from the DOS computer beside my mom, my dad’s Mac in Utah, and the years after. Finding them again brought a lot back. I wanted to share them.</p>
      {storyLive && <a class="arcade-story-link" href={storyPath}>Read how I got here <span aria-hidden="true">↗</span></a>}
      <div class="arcade-status"><span class="arcade-led" aria-hidden="true"></span> Pick a game. Nothing runs until you press play.</div>
    </section>
    <section aria-labelledby="games-heading">
      <div class="arcade-section-heading"><h2 id="games-heading">Choose a game</h2><span>{games.length} games · DOS / Mac / Windows</span></div>
      <div class="arcade-filters" role="group" aria-label="Filter games" hidden>
        {['All', 'DOS', 'Macintosh', 'Windows'].map(platform => <button type="button" data-filter={platform} aria-pressed={platform === 'All'}>{platform}</button>)}
      </div>
      <p class="sr-only" data-filter-status role="status" aria-live="polite"></p>
      <div class="arcade-grid">{games.map((game, index) => <div data-game-platform={game.platform}><ArcadeCard game={game} index={index} /></div>)}</div>
    </section>
    <section class="arcade-disc-section" aria-labelledby="discs-heading">
      <p class="arcade-eyebrow">the discovery</p><h2 id="discs-heading">Or open the whole disc.</h2>
      <p>The search led back to old Mac shareware collections. There’s something about seeing the folders, readmes, and registration notes together. You can explore these discs with a classic Mac desktop.</p>
      <div class="arcade-disc-links">
        <a href="/arcade/discs/arcade-games"><span aria-hidden="true">◉</span><div><strong>MacCube Volume 1</strong><small>Arcade games · Chrysanthemum, Armor, Swoop and more</small></div><span aria-hidden="true">↗</span></a>
        <a href="/arcade/discs/adventure-games"><span aria-hidden="true">◉</span><div><strong>MacCube Volume 2</strong><small>Adventure, card, casino & puzzle · including TaskMaker</small></div><span aria-hidden="true">↗</span></a>
      </div>
    </section>
    <section class="arcade-footnotes" aria-labelledby="more-heading">
      <h2 id="more-heading">More of the story</h2>
      <p>The Tonka games, The Sims, and StarCraft are part of this history too. They aren’t playable here yet.</p>
      <p>The games and their original documentation belong to their creators. The DOS games run with <a href="https://js-dos.com" data-umami-event="outbound-arcade">js-dos</a>; the Mac desktop runs a local build of <a href="https://infinitemac.org" data-umami-event="outbound-arcade">Infinite Mac</a>. The emulators, system disks, games, and shareware CDs are hosted on my own cluster.</p>
      <p>For the computer story after this one: <a href="/blog/how-the-lab-got-here">How the lab got here</a>. There’s more about me at <a href="https://maxfieldallison.com?utm_source=probablyfine&utm_medium=site&utm_campaign=arcade" data-umami-event="outbound-maxfieldallison">maxfieldallison.com</a>.</p>
    </section>
  </div>
</Layout>
<script>
  function setupFilters() {
    const filters = document.querySelector<HTMLElement>('.arcade-filters');
    if (!filters || filters.dataset.bound) return;
    filters.dataset.bound = 'true'; filters.hidden = false;
    filters.querySelectorAll<HTMLButtonElement>('button').forEach(button => button.addEventListener('click', () => {
      filters.querySelectorAll('button').forEach(b => b.setAttribute('aria-pressed', String(b === button)));
      let count = 0;
      document.querySelectorAll<HTMLElement>('[data-game-platform]').forEach(card => {
        card.hidden = button.dataset.filter !== 'All' && card.dataset.gamePlatform !== button.dataset.filter;
        if (!card.hidden) count++;
      });
      const status = document.querySelector('[data-filter-status]');
      if (status) status.textContent = `${count} ${count === 1 ? 'game' : 'games'} shown`;
    }));
  }
  setupFilters(); document.addEventListener('astro:page-load', setupFilters);
</script>
